WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.600
You stream games every night, on Twitch.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.548
But some of your viewers only open YouTube…

3
00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:08.649
and others only watch Kick.

4
00:00:08.649 --> 00:00:12.103
To show up everywhere, you either pick just one…

5
00:00:12.103 --> 00:00:13.758
juggle a bunch of apps…

6
00:00:13.758 --> 00:00:16.821
or pay every month for a cloud relay.

7
00:00:16.921 --> 00:00:20.371
And then it's three chats, in three tabs.

8
00:00:21.171 --> 00:00:27.077
With Corneta, one stream goes from your PC to every platform… no subscription.

9
00:00:27.077 --> 00:00:28.742
Just four steps.

10
00:00:28.742 --> 00:00:31.431
First, click Set it up for me…

11
00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:34.057
and Corneta hooks up OBS.

12
00:00:34.057 --> 00:00:36.240
Next, pick your platforms:

13
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.459
Twitch, YouTube and Kick.

14
00:00:38.459 --> 00:00:42.377
On Twitch and Kick, log in and hit Fetch from account.

15
00:00:42.377 --> 00:00:45.607
On YouTube, Corneta creates the stream.

16
00:00:45.616 --> 00:00:50.602
Then hit GO LIVE… and each platform goes live, one by one.

17
00:00:50.602 --> 00:00:52.435
Each one runs on its own:

18
00:00:52.435 --> 00:00:55.244
if one drops, the rest stay live.

19
00:00:55.244 --> 00:01:01.194
If OBS crashes, with protection on, the BE RIGHT BACK screen holds the stream up.

20
00:01:01.379 --> 00:01:04.267
Finally, all your chats land in one place…

21
00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:06.799
and you reply right from there.

22
00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:11.193
That's it: you're live on all three, with one chat.

23
00:01:11.288 --> 00:01:15.258
After the stream, the report shows how each platform did.

24
00:01:15.258 --> 00:01:18.837
How many people stuck around, where the stream took off…

25
00:01:18.837 --> 00:01:21.538
and the best moments worth clipping.

26
00:01:23.996 --> 00:01:29.388
Go live everywhere. Download free for Windows at corneta.live.
